WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:04.490
The only way to not go crazy
trying to handle responsive images

00:00:04.490 --> 00:00:07.880
is to set up an image pipeline
that makes it easy for

00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:11.720
you to create multiple versions
of your images automatically.

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:14.870
And to do that you're going to
need the right software.

00:00:14.870 --> 00:00:18.050
For your own sanity,
I want you to take a step back and

00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:22.160
install Grunt, ImageOptim,
and ImageMagick.

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:25.030
Seriously, Grunt is super useful.

00:00:25.030 --> 00:00:28.360
I use it all the time to
automate tasks for my projects.

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:31.920
ImageOptim and ImageMagick are also
awesome, because it makes it so

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:36.820
easy to convert images to different
sizes, formats, and compression levels.

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:39.220
You're going to want their help when
you start working on the project for

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:41.980
this course and in your future projects.

00:00:41.980 --> 00:00:45.310
You'll find links in the instructor
notes for some how-to guides.

00:00:45.310 --> 00:00:47.780
Once you've got everything installed,
check this box to continue.

